<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Huh.3F">Huh?</span></h2>
<p>This "discussion" appears to be nothing more than a duplication of sections arbitrarily copied (not moved) from <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Talk%20-%20Main%20Page" title="Talk:Main Page">Talk:Main_Page</a>.  In addition the actual "primary discussion forum" for wiki editors is presumably the <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://social.bioware.com/group/239/">Dragon Age Toolset Wiki Editors</a> group.  So what is the actual role of the Community Portal page going to be? It's all very well for someone to randomly declare it to be X but if we have no intention to use it for X then it is redundant and/or misleading.  I have started a <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://social.bioware.com/group/239/discussion/2016/">thread</a> to discuss this further  --<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20Sunjammer" title="User:Sunjammer">Sunjammer</a> 21:30, 26 November 2009 (UTC)
</p>
